<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vushmgir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 967</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Vushmgir ibn Ziyar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vushmgir ibn Ziyar was the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardavij">Mardavij</a> and ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziyarid-dynasty">Ziyarid dynasty</a> from 935 to 967. He held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorgan">Gorgan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a>, shifting his allegiance between them, but lost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jibal">Jibal</a> to the Buyids. He was killed by a wild boar while hunting in 967 and was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qabus">Qabus ibn Vushmgir</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vushmgir.jpg" alt="Vushmgir" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: چوپان راستگو · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GONBAD25.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
